  "findings": [
    "Node reports real before/after vm contexts with names/origins and evaluates within contextId. Verified Home emits only its current owner and fails the first named-realm assertion.",
    "Pinned JSC JSGlobalObjectRuntimeAgent explicitly rejects execution-context IDs because it owns one global. A real port needs native realm registry/controller routing and lifecycle handling.",
    "Recovery source retains name/origin in their original getter order without changing NodeVM public header layout, adds weak realm metadata and owner-loop retirement, and drafts per-realm controller channels with opaque remote-object remapping. No completed build/runtime credit.",
    "First compile failed from the helper declaration in Bun versus definition in Bun::NodeVM. The repaired declaration is preserved remotely. Repair builds refused at disk admission; logs retain actual 1468/1288 MB values."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Remote-object argument routing, exception object mapping, object-group release, native realm-controller roots/lifetimes, post-destruction pointer reuse, owner teardown, all platforms and full suite need implementation/verification before landing.",
    "The original public NodeVM header was restored byte-identically; no ABI guard relaxation is used. Both recovery commits are preserved, including the initial draft that changed a signature.",
    "Source remains excluded from main. Existing #428/#66/#885 and original inspector conflict #886 remain open."
  ],
